  "title": "How to Pass Creación Digital II — UEM 2026-27",
  "slides": [
    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital II</h1><h2>Universidad Europea de Madrid · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h total · 80 h presencial contact · 70 h autonomous/tutoring/evaluation</em></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official course contract</h2><table><tr><th>Subject</th><td>Creación Digital II</td></tr><tr><th>Contact structure</th><td>10 h magistral · 20 h seminars · 8 h problem solving · 20 h projects · 14 h labs · 8 h debates</td></tr><tr><th>Contents</th><td>II.1–II.6: retouching, avatars, digital fashion experiences, video editing, web/portfolio, holograms and AR</td></tr></table>"},
    {"content":"<h2>How you pass</h2><p>You pass by developing a visible design process from brief to critique to final artefact. The portfolio is not a gallery alone: it is a reconstructable record of decisions, sources, files, and human authorship.</p><ul><li>Conceptual seminar and debate evidence</li><li>Studio lab artefact with source/process folder</li><li>Individual problem-solving drills</li><li>Project report and critique</li></ul>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Wave 1 — II.5 Web and portfolio</h2><p>Build a local portfolio page or small static site that presents your own work and its process. Use semantic structure, accessible media alternatives, attribution, file-format discipline, and an AI-use declaration where relevant. A public showroom URL is optional and requires the exhibition gate.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Evidence status</h2><p>Anwar and Rizzi ground authorship and studio-AI framing. Fashion-portfolio web-UX pedagogy remains NONE/[UNVERIFIED-GAP]; this is a declared pilot, not a claim that a layout pattern causes employability outcomes. Other II units retain their matrix-specific NONE or [BIBLIO-GAP] status.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Consent and public work</h2><p>Teaching may proceed with private/local artefacts. Research data collection and public exhibition are OFF until signed consent, DPO/institutional approval, and administration are complete. S1/S2 checklists are unsigned templates only.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Evaluation and completion</h2><p>Follow the official UEM guide and current subject documentation for binding weights and dates. Submit the artefact, process evidence, report, and individual problem-solving evidence. Resubmission must repair the missing evidence explicitly.</p>"}
